      "id": "prismtail",
      "name": "Prismtail",
      "description": "Colour occupies the part of the hair nearest the horse and stops before the ends, which always come back to the hair's own colour. Within that run it is stacked in bands, widest at the top and compressing downward, four to seven of them, and the boundaries between adjacent bands are soft - the hues blend rather than cut. The order is the spectrum's own and never repeats or reverses; a short run drops bands off the top rather than squeezing all seven in. Beside the mane's coloured section the upper neck carries a soft wash in the last of those hues, at a fraction of the saturation, with a scatter of pale points in it.",
